# VDI agent startup, step by step (Jupyter + VS Code only)

**Scope:** what the Coder agent does at workspace start so the KasmVNC desktop shows two
working icons — **JupyterLab** and **VS Code**. Airflow/IntelliJ later follow the same pattern.
**Implements:** ADR-0002 (`docs/adr/0002-vdi-desktop-via-kasmvnc-and-bounce.md`).
**Status:** logic proven in the POC (Debian + UBI 9, KasmVNC 1.5.0, no sudo for `coder`);
the icon-fetch/generation steps and the no-auto-lock image changes below are the
target form, not yet in the templates/Dockerfile.

## Division of labour

| Baked into the image (`Dockerfile.ubi`) | Done by the agent at start |
|---|---|
| XFCE, Chromium (`chromium-browser`), VS Code RPM, JupyterLab venv (`/opt/jupyter`) | Create per-user dirs (`~/Desktop`, `~/.local/share/{applications,icons}`, `~/bin`) |
| KasmVNC RPM + `kasmvncserver` symlink, `VERSION_CODENAME` in `/etc/os-release`, coder-owned `/usr/share/kasmvnc/www` | Fetch app icons from the Coder server |
| Wrapper scripts master copy (`/usr/local/share/poc/launch-jupyter`, `launch-vscode`) | Generate the two `.desktop` files, copy wrappers to `~/bin`, mark launchers trusted |
| **No auto-lock**: `xfce4-screensaver` removed; xfconf defaults disable screensaver/lock/DPMS (see “No auto-lock” below) | — (nothing: agent script has no session D-Bus, so this cannot be done reliably at start) |

Rules: the image never changes per user; the startup script is **idempotent** (runs on every
start, safe to re-run); nothing is downloaded except two small SVGs; no sudo.

## Sequence

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A["1. Agent connects; kasmvnc module script and<br/>agent startup_script run (order not guaranteed)"] --> B["2. mkdir per-user dirs"]
  B --> C["3. Fetch icons: GET {coder}/icon/jupyter.svg, code.svg"]
  C --> D["4. Copy wrappers launch-jupyter / launch-vscode to ~/bin"]
  D --> E["5. Write JupyterLab.desktop + VSCode.desktop<br/>(applications menu + Desktop)"]
  E --> F["6. chmod +x + trusted metadata"]
  F --> G["7. XFCE picks icons up (xfdesktop watches ~/Desktop;<br/>works whether icons land before or after session start)"]
  G --> H["8. User clicks icon -> wrapper starts service if needed -> app window opens"]
```

Why order-tolerance matters: Coder does not guarantee the module's `coder_script` runs
before/after `coder_agent.startup_script`. xfdesktop monitors `~/Desktop`, so icons appear
even if the desktop session started first. The startup script must therefore never fail
the agent if the desktop is not up yet — it only writes files.

## The steps

### 1. Inputs

- `data.coder_workspace.me.access_url` — base URL for the icon fetch (public static files,
  no token needed). Fallback if unset: the baked icons in the image.
- `$HOME` = `/home/coder` (persistent volume — files survive restarts, so steps are cheap no-ops after first start).

### 2. Create directories

```bash
mkdir -p "$HOME/Desktop" "$HOME/.local/share/applications" \
         "$HOME/.local/share/icons" "$HOME/bin"
```

### 3. Fetch icons from Coder

Coder serves 150 built-in icons at `/icon/<name>.svg`, the same set `coder_app.icon` uses —
so desktop artwork matches the portal exactly.

```bash
for i in jupyter code; do
  curl -fsSL "${CODER_ACCESS_URL}/icon/$i.svg" -o "$HOME/.local/share/icons/$i.svg" || true
done
```

`|| true`: a failed fetch must not fail startup; XFCE falls back to a generic icon.

### 4. Install wrappers

```bash
cp /usr/local/share/poc/launch-jupyter /usr/local/share/poc/launch-vscode "$HOME/bin/"
chmod +x "$HOME/bin/launch-jupyter" "$HOME/bin/launch-vscode"
```

Wrapper behaviour (unchanged from POC):

- `launch-jupyter`: if `127.0.0.1:8888/lab` is down, start `/opt/jupyter/bin/jupyter lab`
  (no Jupyter token — localhost only, Coder/Kasm is the auth boundary), wait for health,
  then `chromium-browser --no-sandbox --disable-gpu --password-store=basic --app=http://127.0.0.1:8888/lab`
  (browser binary resolves `chromium` on Debian, `chromium-browser` on EL).
- `launch-vscode`: `code --no-sandbox --password-store=basic /home/coder`
  (`--no-sandbox` is mandatory in containers; `--password-store=basic` on both wrappers
  avoids GNOME keyring “set a password” prompts — the `coder` user has no password).

### 5. Generate the `.desktop` files

Written to **both** `~/.local/share/applications/` (menu/App Finder) and `~/Desktop/` (desktop icons):

```ini
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=JupyterLab
Icon=/home/coder/.local/share/icons/jupyter.svg
Exec=/home/coder/bin/launch-jupyter
Terminal=false
Categories=Development;
```

```ini
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=VS Code
Icon=/home/coder/.local/share/icons/code.svg
Exec=/home/coder/bin/launch-vscode
Terminal=false
Categories=Development;
```

### 6. Make launchers trusted

```bash
chmod +x "$HOME/Desktop/"*.desktop "$HOME/.local/share/applications/"*.desktop
for f in "$HOME/Desktop/"*.desktop; do gio set "$f" metadata::trusted true 2>/dev/null || true; done
```

Without the executable bit (and ideally the trusted flag) XFCE shows generic/untrusted
icons — the cosmetic issue seen in the POC.

### 7. Desktop pickup

No restart needed: xfdesktop watches `~/Desktop`. Nothing in the startup script touches
`DISPLAY` (the script runs outside the desktop session).

### 8. Click behaviour

- First Jupyter click starts the server (~seconds), subsequent clicks just open/focus the app window (wrapper's health check sees 8888 up).
- VS Code opens directly; both apps run on display `:1` (the Kasm session) because the icon launches inside it.

## Proposed `startup_script` (target form)

```hcl
resource "coder_agent" "main" {
  # ... display_apps { web_terminal = false ... } ...

  startup_script = <<-EOT
    set -u
    ICON_DIR="$HOME/.local/share/icons"
    mkdir -p "$HOME/Desktop" "$HOME/.local/share/applications" "$ICON_DIR" "$HOME/bin"

    for i in jupyter code; do
      curl -fsSL "${data.coder_workspace.me.access_url}/icon/$i.svg" -o "$ICON_DIR/$i.svg" || true
    done

    cp /usr/local/share/poc/launch-jupyter /usr/local/share/poc/launch-vscode "$HOME/bin/"

    cat > "$HOME/.local/share/applications/JupyterLab.desktop" <<'EOF'
    [Desktop Entry]
    Type=Application
    Name=JupyterLab
    Icon=/home/coder/.local/share/icons/jupyter.svg
    Exec=/home/coder/bin/launch-jupyter
    Terminal=false
    Categories=Development;
    EOF

    cat > "$HOME/.local/share/applications/VSCode.desktop" <<'EOF'
    [Desktop Entry]
    Type=Application
    Name=VS Code
    Icon=/home/coder/.local/share/icons/code.svg
    Exec=/home/coder/bin/launch-vscode
    Terminal=false
    Categories=Development;
    EOF

    cp "$HOME/.local/share/applications/JupyterLab.desktop" "$HOME/.local/share/applications/VSCode.desktop" "$HOME/Desktop/"
    chmod +x "$HOME/bin/launch-"* "$HOME/Desktop/"*.desktop "$HOME/.local/share/applications/"*.desktop
    for f in "$HOME/Desktop/"*.desktop; do gio set "$f" metadata::trusted true 2>/dev/null || true; done
  EOT
}
```

(Watch Terraform heredoc escaping in real code: `$HOME` is fine, but any `${...}` meant for
bash must be written `$${...}`. The `gio` binary comes with glib2 — verify it exists in the
UBI image, else skip step 6's second half.)

## No auto-lock, no password prompts (image level)

**Problem.** The XFCE image ships `xfce4-screensaver` (autostarted) and
`xfce4-power-manager` (DPMS blanking). The `coder` user is created **without a
password**, so a locked session can never be unlocked — the VDI is dead until
restart. The same no-password user makes Chromium/VS Code pop GNOME keyring
“set a password” prompts.

**Decision.** No screen lock inside the VDI. The auth boundary is Coder/Kasm
(SSO + app-only cookie) plus the user's endpoint OS lock; a lock with a shared
or nonexistent password adds no security, only lockouts. Idle control, if
required, belongs server-side (Kasm idle disconnect, workspace autostop).

**Fix — all in the image** (the agent script cannot do this: `xfconf-query`
needs the running session's D-Bus):

```dockerfile
# 1. Remove the screensaver entirely (nothing to autostart or lock)
RUN dnf -y remove xfce4-screensaver
```

```xml
<!-- 2. /etc/xdg/xfce4/xfconf/xfce-perchannel-xml/xfce4-screensaver.xml
        (belt & braces if the package ever returns) -->
<channel name="xfce4-screensaver" version="1.0">
  <property name="saver" type="empty">
    <property name="enabled" type="bool" value="false"/>
  </property>
  <property name="lock" type="empty">
    <property name="enabled" type="bool" value="false"/>
  </property>
</channel>
```

```xml
<!-- 3. /etc/xdg/xfce4/xfconf/xfce-perchannel-xml/xfce4-power-manager.xml
        (never blank the display either — a black screen looks like a lock) -->
<channel name="xfce4-power-manager" version="1.0">
  <property name="xfce4-power-manager" type="empty">
    <property name="dpms-enabled" type="bool" value="false"/>
    <property name="blank-on-ac" type="int" value="0"/>
  </property>
</channel>
```

Files under `/etc/xdg` are xfconf *system defaults*: read at session start,
valid for fresh home volumes, still user-overridable. And the wrappers carry
`--password-store=basic` (step 4) so no keyring prompt appears.

## Validation checklist

```bash
ls ~/Desktop ~/.local/share/applications ~/.local/share/icons   # both .desktop + both .svg
curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8888/lab                              # after clicking Jupyter (or running ~/bin/launch-jupyter)
pgrep -f '/usr/share/code/code'                                 # after clicking VS Code
curl -sf http://<coder>/icon/jupyter.svg -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n'   # icon endpoint reachable (200)
```

Plus the agent-level checks from the POC: agent `running ready`, `kasm-vnc (healthy)`,
module log ends with `KasmVNC server started successfully!`, `sudo -n true` refused for `coder`.

Anti-lock checks:

```bash
rpm -q xfce4-screensaver        # package not found
pgrep -a xfce4-screensaver      # nothing running in the session
grep -A2 'name="lock"' /etc/xdg/xfce4/xfconf/xfce-perchannel-xml/xfce4-screensaver.xml
# leave the desktop idle past the old timeout: no lock prompt, display stays on
```

## Troubleshooting (all seen in the POC)

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Module dies instantly, agent `start_error` | `VERSION_CODENAME: unbound variable` (script uses `set -u`, UBI lacks it) | `echo 'VERSION_CODENAME=""' >> /etc/os-release` in image |
| Module tries to install Kasm and fails on `rhel` | `kasmvncserver` not on PATH | Bake the Oracle 9 RPM in + `/usr/bin/kasmvncserver` symlink (module then skips install) |
| `mv: ... path_vnc.html: Permission denied` | Path-app patch writes to Kasm web root without sudo | `chown` `/usr/share/kasmvnc/www` to `coder` in image |
| Jupyter window opens black / dies | Chromium sandbox in container | `--no-sandbox --disable-gpu` in wrapper |
| Generic document icons | Launcher not executable/trusted, or icon fetch failed | Step 6; check the two SVGs exist and `Icon=` paths are absolute |
| `apt-get update` fails during module install (Debian) | VS Code .deb left an unsigned Microsoft repo | Remove `vscode.sources` after install (image) — not applicable once Kasm is baked in |
| Screen locks / goes black after idle, asks for a password | `xfce4-screensaver` lock or DPMS blanking; `coder` has no password to unlock with | Remove screensaver + xfconf defaults (see “No auto-lock”) |
| “Set password for new keyring” prompt in VS Code/Chromium | GNOME keyring with a password-less user | `--password-store=basic` on both wrappers |

## Out of scope (same pattern later)

- Airflow icon (`/icon/airflow.svg`, wrapper to `127.0.0.1:8080`), IntelliJ (`/icon/intellij.svg`)
- Panel/dock pinning (XFCE panel config in `~/.config/xfce4/panel/`) — desktop + menu entries are enough for now
- Per-team icon sets via template parameters
